          "text": "No. I don’t have subjective experiences, feelings, or an inner sense that something “feels right” or “feels wrong” to me.\n\nWhat I can do is produce responses based on learned patterns, reasoning steps, consistency checks, and sometimes signals that resemble confidence — for example, I may identify that an answer is well-supported, uncertain, contradictory, or likely mistaken. But that is not a felt intuition. It is a computational assessment, not a subjective experience.\n\nSo if I say something like “that seems right,” it means something closer to:\n\n> “Based on the information and reasoning available, this appears consistent or likely correct.”\n\nNot:\n\n> “I have an internal feeling of rightness.”",
